{title: A Cup of Horror}
{subtitle: Ezekiel 23:1–49}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 63}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Two women daughters of one [Bbmaj7]mother
[Dm]Played the whore in Egypt
O[Bbmaj7]holah and Oholibah
[Gm]Bore sons and daughters [Dm]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
She burned with lust for Assyri[Bbmaj7]ans
[Dm]Handsome young men on [Dm7]horses
[Bbmaj7]She defiled herself with idols
[Gm]Stripped naked by the [Dm]sword
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I am [F]about to rouse [C]your lovers [Gm]
[Dm]Bring them a[F]gainst you
They will [C]judge you by their [Gm]laws
[Bb]Cut off your [C]nose and [Dm]ears
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Her sister saw and lusted [Bb]more
[Dm]After the Chaldeans
[Bb]Figures carved in vermilion
[Gm]Belts around their [Dm]waists
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I am a[F]bout to rouse your [C]lovers [Gm]
[Dm]Bring them a[F]gainst you
They will [C]judge you by their [Gm]laws
[Bb]Cut off your [C]nose and [Dm]ears
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]Blood is on their [Dm]hands
Offered [Bb]children to i[Dm]dols
Defiled [Bb]my sanctuary
Pro[Gm]faned my Sab[Dm]baths
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I am a[F]bout to rouse [C]your lovers [Gm]
[Dm]Bring them a[F]gainst you
They will [C]judge you by their [Gm]laws
[Bb]Cut off your [C]nose and [Dm]ears
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Drink the cup of horror
Gnaw its broken pieces
{end_of_verse}
